<title>USA: U.S. final Q4 GDP rose 3.8 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. final Q4 GDP rose 3.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce seasonally adjusted GDP data on a chain-weighted basis. Following are annualized percent changes from prior quarters, in 1992 chain dollars.</p>
<p>    -			     Q4-F---Q4-P---Q3-F---1996</p>
<p> Gross Domestic Product	3.8    3.9    2.1    2.4</p>
<p> Final Sales Domest.Product  4.9    5.0    0.5    2.7</p>
<p> GDP Price Index		 1.9    1.8    2.0    2.1</p>
<p> Implicit Price Deflator     1.5    1.4    1.7    2.0</p>
<p> Consumer Spending	     3.4    3.4    0.5    2.5</p>
<p> -Durable Goods		  5.0    4.1   -2.6    5.4</p>
<p> -Nondurable Goods	     1.8    1.4    0.4    1.4</p>
<p>Pct Change,'92 chain dollars: Q4-F---Q4-P---Q3-F---1996</p>
<p> Consumer Spending-Services  3.8    4.3    1.3    2.4</p>
<p> Business Investment	   5.5    5.5   17.5    7.4</p>
<p> Housing Investment	   -1.8   -0.4   -5.2    5.3</p>
<p> Exports of Goods/Svcs	25.0   24.8   -0.9    6.5</p>
<p> Imports of Goods/Svcs	 3.3    3.8    9.3    6.4</p>
<p> Govt.Purchases/Investment  -0.9   -0.4   -0.6    0.8</p>
<p> -Federal			 -5.3   -4.9   -3.5   -1.1</p>
<p> -State and Local		1.9    2.4    1.1    2.0</p>
<p>Note: Advance (A) is first estimate, Preliminary (P) is second estimate, and Final (F) is last estimate for the quarter.</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted annual rates, in blns of '92 chain dollars:</p>
<p>    -				Q4-F-----Q4-P-----Q3-F----1996</p>
<p> Gross Domestic Product   6,993.6  6,994.4  6,928.4  6,907.2</p>
<p> Final Sales Dom.Product  6,975.9  6,977.4  6,892.7  6,892.1</p>
<p> Consumer Spending	  4,732.5  4,733.3  4,693.5  4,690.7</p>
<p> -Durable Goods		 619.1    617.8    611.6    611.4</p>
<p> -NonDurable Goods	  1,448.6  1,447.4  1,442.2  1,442.0</p>
<p> -Services		    2,665.6  2,668.7  2,640.6  2,638.3</p>
<p> Business Investment	  792.0    791.8    781.4    766.8</p>
<p> Housing Investment	   276.6    277.6    277.8    276.7</p>
<p>A-Advance. P-Preliminary. F-Final.</p>
<p> Blns of '92 chain dollars:     Q4-F-----Q4-P-----Q3-F-----1996</p>
<p> Business Inventory Change   17.3     16.4     34.5     14.0</p>
<p> -NonFarm			  19.3     18.4     34.6     17.1</p>
<p> -Farm			     -2.3     -2.4     -0.4     -3.6</p>
<p> Net Exports Goods/Svcs     -98.4   -100.0   -137.4   -113.6</p>
<p> -Exports			 862.9    862.5    816.1    825.9</p>
<p> -Imports			 961.3    962.5    953.5    939.5</p>
<p> Government Purchases     1,273.4  1,274.8  1,276.1  1,270.6</p>
<p> -Federal			 462.9    463.4    469.3    467.1</p>
<p> -State and Local	     811.4    812.4    807.7    804.3</p>
<p>A-Advance. P-Preliminary. F-Final.</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had expected the final estimate of the fourth quarter GDP estimate to show a 4.0 percent increase, the price index to be up 1.8 percent and the implicit deflator to rise 1.4 percent.</p>
<p>The department revised its total for gross domestic product in 1996 from $6,607.4 billion to $6,907.2 billion. The change did not affect the 2.4 percent increase for the year.</p>
<p>Commerce also said that final sales to domestic purchasers rose 2.6 percent in the fourth quarter to $7,070.3 billion.</p>
